{
  "name": "Screen CVs from an n8n form against your job description with Gemini and Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Screen CVs from an n8n form against your job description with Gemini and Google Sheets\n\nCollect applications through a hosted n8n form, read each PDF CV, and let Google Gemini score it against your job description. Every candidate lands in Google Sheets with a 0-100 score, a recommendation and the must-haves they meet or miss, so you only open the CVs worth reading.\n\n### How it works\n1. Candidates fill in the **Job application form** (name, email, PDF CV, optional note).\n2. **Extract text from CV** reads the PDF. Scanned or image-only PDFs are flagged instead of scored.\n3. **Score CV against job description** compares the CV with the role you set and returns structured JSON. The prompt ignores protected characteristics and only judges job evidence.\n4. The result is appended to your Google Sheet and the candidate sees a thank-you page.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add a free **Google Gemini (PaLM) API** credential (key from aistudio.google.com).\n2. Create a Google Sheet with a `Candidates` tab and this header row: `submitted_at, name, email, score, recommendation, summary, must_haves_met, must_haves_missing, strengths, gaps, years_experience, red_flags, location, note, cv_filename`.\n3. Put the Sheet ID in **Set job description** and connect your **Google Sheets** credential.\n4. Paste your role into **Set job description**.\n5. Activate the workflow and share the form's production URL in your job ad.\n\n### Customization\n- Change the scoring rules or thresholds in **Score CV against job description**.\n- Sort the sheet by `score` or add a filter view for `shortlist`.\n\nFailure alerts: fill in the alert node in **Alert on errors** and choose this workflow under **Settings > Error workflow**.",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 600
      },
      "id": "de5f1ae5-67c9-5a8a-ad52-3863fd16f009",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
